    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000001": {
      "name": "What a flash flood is",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "flash-flood-explainer.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "## What a flash flood is\n\n**A river in flood after rain rises over hours or days. This kind arrives in\nminutes, because the water was not falling from the sky. It was released all at\nonce, high up.**\n\n![How this kind of flood starts, and why it is called flash](attachment:flash-flood-explainer.png)\n\nFour things follow from that, and the rest of the story is built on them.\n\n**It is fast.** There is no slow build to watch for. The rise reported at\nGalchhi, 90 km down the valley, was\n**+9 m in half an hour**.\n\n**It is heavy.** This is not clean water. A surge like this carries mud,\nboulders and trees, and that is what takes out bridges and roads, rather than\nthe water alone.\n\n**It makes noise.** A mass that size moving down a valley shakes the ground hard\nenough for a seismometer to record it. That is why the first report of this\nflood was an earthquake alert, and why the story can be followed at all.\n\n**It happens again.** ICIMOD notes that the same side stream\n[flooded twice in fourteen months](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/major-flash-flood-sweeps-through-nepals-rasuwa-district-raising-fears-of-further-downstream-flooding/), the earlier one hitting the\nsame border crossing. That is the difference between an accident and a hazard,\nand it is the argument for watching a valley like this one.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What a flash flood is"
        },
        "extent": [
          9256882.117232194,
          3081345.6937492713,
          9711959.114141138,
          3416601.8856210187
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.4,
            "targetLayer": "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": true
          },
          {
            "opacity": 1.0,
            "targetLayer": "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
            "visible": false
          },
          {
