    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000002": {
      "name": "Filed as an earthquake, then relabelled",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**It was published as \"earthquake, magnitude 5.2\", then relabelled\n\"landslide\".**\n\nThe red dot is the official record, [us7000tbwb](https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/eventpage/us7000tbwb), from the US\nGeological Survey. It marks where the shaking was calculated from, not where the\nice fell, so read it as a neighbourhood rather than an address.\n\n**On the map:** \ud83d\udd34 the seismic solution, worked back from the shaking\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The first alert was wrong"
        },
