    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000003": {
      "name": "How far the shaking travelled",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**The grey bands are distance from the collapse: 10, 25 and 50 kilometres.**\n\nThey are real distances on the ground, not circles drawn on the screen, so they\nstay true wherever the map stretches. Grey, because distance is not damage.\n\n**On the map:** the grey bands are 0-10, 10-25 and 25-50 km from the source \u00b7 \ud83d\udd34 the source \u00b7 \u26ab the seismometer, just outside them\n",
