    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000005": {
      "name": "Why the recording says flood, not earthquake",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "kkn-seismogram.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "## Why the recording says flood, not earthquake\n\n**Two things in this recording do not belong to an earthquake: it started\nslowly, and it never stopped.**\n\n![Ground motion recorded at NK.KKN](attachment:kkn-seismogram.png)\n\nThree views of the same ninety minutes:\n\n- **top**: the ground moving up and down\n- **middle**: how strong that movement is compared with a quiet moment before\n- **bottom**: which frequencies are shaking, where bright means strong\n\n**It started slowly.** The shaking took **40 seconds**\nto build to its peak. A fault breaking arrives all at once, like a hammer blow.\n\n**It never stopped.** The peak reached **49 dB** above the\nquiet background before the event, and an hour later the ground at Kakani was\nstill about **11 dB** above it. A magnitude 5.2 earthquake\ngoes quiet within minutes.\n\nA third clue sat in the catalogue entry itself: the magnitude was measured from\n*surface waves*, the slow waves that run along the ground rather than through\nit. All of it fits a mass of ice, rock and water moving down a valley and making\nnoise the whole way, which is what analysts read when they relabelled the event.\n\nICIMOD reports that a seismometer at Jilong, [about 12 km from the affected\narea](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/major-flash-flood-sweeps-through-nepals-rasuwa-district-raising-fears-of-further-downstream-flooding/), showed anomalous signals too.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Why the recording says flood, not earthquake"
        },
        "extent": [
          9375997.964408983,
          3157740.752158188,
          9637371.063282128,
          3350294.8702110113
        ],
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "opacity": 0.4,
            "targetLayer": "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "opacity": 1.0,
