    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000008": {
      "name": "This has happened before",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "## This has happened before\n\n**The same side stream flooded twice in fourteen months.**\n\nICIMOD notes that the Lhende Khola, the stream in the segment above, had\nalready [flooded once in the fourteen months before this](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/major-flash-flood-sweeps-through-nepals-rasuwa-district-raising-fears-of-further-downstream-flooding/), and\nthat the earlier flood hit the same border crossing.\n\nTwo years before that, above **Thame** in the Everest region, a rock avalanche\nfell into a glacial lake at 4,900 m. The lake breached, the wave breached a\nsecond lake below it, and [459,000 cubic metres of water](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/everest-region-a-hotspot-of-cryosphere-linked-hazards-icimods-new-study-on-nepals-2024-thame-flood-confirms/) carried\nboulders **80 km** downstream. [Fourteen properties were destroyed](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/glof-from-thyanbo-glacial-lake-sweeps-away-thame-village/),\namong them one school and one health post.\n\nNepal has recorded [more than 90 of these floods since the early 1920s](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/everest-region-a-hotspot-of-cryosphere-linked-hazards-icimods-new-study-on-nepals-2024-thame-flood-confirms/),\nand the Everest region alone five significant ones in under fifty years. ICIMOD\ncounts [47 potentially dangerous glacial lakes](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/glof-from-thyanbo-glacial-lake-sweeps-away-thame-village/) and projects a\nthree-fold increase in the risk by the end of the century.\n\nWarming is making more of these lakes, and loosening more of the rock that falls\ninto them.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "This has happened before"
        },
        "extent": [
          9390688.874802431,
          3190398.6464202357,
          9618227.373256901,
          3358026.7423561094
        ],
