    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000009": {
      "name": "The riverbed drops 2,215 m, and most of it early",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {
            "valley-profile.png": {
              "image/png": ""
            }
          },
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "## The riverbed drops 2,215 m, and most of it early\n\n**The first 20 km of riverbed fall 42.5 m every\nkilometre. The last 100 km fall 1.9 m.**\n\n![Height of the riverbed, from the source to the plain](attachment:valley-profile.png)\n\nRead it left to right: the source on the left, the plain on the right. The line\nis the height of the riverbed, sampled every\n200 m from the same terrain the map shades.\n\nThe first figure is steep. The second is nearly flat. On the steep part the\nwater arrives as a wall; on the flat part it arrives as a rise. That is what the\nnext segment colours the channel by.\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The riverbed drops 2,215 m, and most of it early"
        },
        "extent": [
          9256882.117232194,
          3081345.6937492713,
