    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000014": {
      "name": "What a flood like this takes out",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**Reporting counts [at least 19 bridges destroyed](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/27/nepal-tibet-floods-what-happened-what-caused-them-and-who-is-missing) near the\nborder, without saying over what stretch of river.**\n\nThe nearest bridge OpenStreetMap has is **42 km** down,\nbelow the damage. Neither number divides into the other.\n\nFurther down, **438 schools** and **103 health posts**\nstand within 3 km of the water. Every mark here is something the flood could\nreach, not something reported damaged.\n\n**On the map:** pink dots are bridges \u00b7 green are schools and health posts \u00b7 the brown line is the valley road\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "What a flood like this takes out"
        },
        "extent": [
          9430209.290047824,
          3203357.036679911,
