    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000016": {
      "name": "The river rose nine metres in half an hour",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "map",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "**ICIMOD reported 9 m at Galchhi, km\n90, and 7 m at\nMalekhu, km 115.**\n\nBoth sit in the flat lower reach, where a flood shows up as a river level rising\nrather than as a wall of water arriving.\n\n**On the map:** \ud83d\udd35 where a river level was reported \u00b7 the two short dark lines are where the valley was measured across\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "The river rose nine metres in half an hour"
        },
