    "0b6c1a10-0000-4000-8001-000000000021": {
      "name": "Sources",
      "parameters": {
        "content": {
          "attachments": {},
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "markdown": "## Sources\n\n**Nothing here is drawn by hand,** and every feature\ncarries its own source, link, licence and fetch date, so a layer copied into\nanother map still says what it is.\n\n**Fetched or measured**\n\n- Seismic record: [USGS us7000tbwb](https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/eventpage/us7000tbwb), public domain.\n- Ground motion: NK.KKN via [EarthScope](https://service.earthscope.org/).\n- Rivers, tributaries, places, hydropower, bridges, schools, health posts,\n  roads and the basemap: [OpenStreetMap](https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright), ODbL 1.0.\n- Terrain, profile, reach gradients, cross-sections:\n  [Terrarium tiles](https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/), AWS Open Data.\n- Population: [WorldPop](https://www.worldpop.org/) Nepal 2026,\n  constrained 100 m, CC BY 4.0.\n\n**Quoted from reporting**\n\n- [ICIMOD, 26 August 2026](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/major-flash-flood-sweeps-through-nepals-rasuwa-district-raising-fears-of-further-downstream-flooding/): the river levels at Galchhi and\n  Malekhu, the Bhote Koshi rising around 09:00, the Jilong seismometer, and the\n  Lhende Khola flooding twice in fourteen months.\n- [Al Jazeera, 27 August 2026](https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/27/nepal-tibet-floods-what-happened-what-caused-them-and-who-is-missing): the 08:40 onset, 19 bridges\n  destroyed, about 40 km of road washed away.\n- ICIMOD on Thame 2024: [fourteen properties, one school, one health\n  post](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/glof-from-thyanbo-glacial-lake-sweeps-away-thame-village/) and [459,000 cubic metres, 80 km of debris, more than 90\n  such floods since the 1920s](https://www.icimod.org/press-release/everest-region-a-hotspot-of-cryosphere-linked-hazards-icimods-new-study-on-nepals-2024-thame-flood-confirms/).\n- Background: [2026 Nepal floods](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nepal_floods), CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\n**Worked out here, and labelled wherever it appears**\n\nThe reaches, the distance rings and the Gandak-Ganga junction. The two\ncross-section widths. The population totals, which are modelled, not counted.\nAnd every arrival time below Timure: only the first leg is anchored on reported\ntimes, and the rest is that leg scaled by bed gradient, which is crude and\ncrudest on the flat.\n\n**What is deliberately missing**\n\nNo flood outline, no damage layer, no casualty data. Copernicus was activated as\n**EMSR927** with products still to come, and an invented outline is worse than\nan honest gap. The bridges, schools and health posts here are things the flood\ncould **reach**, not things reported damaged.\n\n",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "34%",
          "title": "Sources, and how to rebuild this"
        },
        "extent": [
          9256882.117232194,
          3081345.6937492713,
          9711959.114141138,
          3416601.8856210187
        ],
